WEBVTT

00:00:02.764 --> 00:00:10.691
The handwheel: hub, thin web, rim. The blank was made with Revolution as in lesson 6. The web needs 5 lightening holes

00:00:10.691 --> 00:00:22.691
Draw just one: sketch on XY, centre on the vertical axis, diameter 20; then lock it 30 from the centre

00:00:28.792 --> 00:00:40.792
Pocket: type Through all, tick Reversed—the sketch is on the bottom face, so reversed cuts into the part

00:00:41.892 --> 00:00:53.844
Select the pocket and click Polar pattern: the axis defaults to the sketch normal (the wheel axis); 5 occurrences over 360°

00:00:53.844 --> 00:01:02.760
Five holes evenly spaced. Change the count and the holes follow; change the original hole and all five change
